<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Council of Castile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1385–1834</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Royal Council of Castile</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> was the chief governing council of the Crown of Castile, created by John I in 1385 and reorganised by Isabella I and Ferdinand II in 1480 with a majority of university-trained lawyers. It acted as supreme court and administrative body for justice and internal government, and under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> headed their system of councils. It was abolished in 1834.</p></div>
